# =============================================================================
# Docker build context — Hacker Dojo SERVER API image.
#
# This is an ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list. Everything is excluded by `*` on the
# first line, and only what the server build actually needs is added back.
#
# The reason is the secrets requirement rather than context size. A deny-list
# fails OPEN: every credential, cache and build artefact that lands in this
# repository next month is sent to the daemon unless somebody remembers to add
# a pattern for it. An allow-list fails CLOSED — a new file is excluded until
# it is deliberately named.
#
# That matters here specifically, because this tree currently holds a live
# Stripe secret key and the Supabase service-role key (server/.env), two more
# environment files (mobile/.env, supabase/.env), an Android signing keystore,
# and supabase/.temp/start-secrets/ generated by the local Supabase stack.
#
# Note the distinction: this file controls what the DAEMON CAN SEE. What ends
# up in the image is decided by the Dockerfile's COPY instructions. Both
# matter, and this is the half that governs secret exposure.
# =============================================================================

# Exclude everything.
*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include exactly what the server image is built from.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The npm workspace root. Both are mandatory: `npm ci` installs from the
# lockfile, and the lockfile is what makes the install reproducible.
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# The API itself — src/, package.json, tsconfig.json, tsconfig.build.json.
# Its .env, dist/ and node_modules are re-excluded below.
!server

# The mobile workspace MANIFEST ONLY, never its source.
#
# Verified empirically: `npm ci` succeeds without this file, both scoped
# (--workspace server) and unscoped, because it resolves from the lockfile and
# does not re-read workspace manifests. It is kept regardless — it costs ~2 KB,
# contains no secrets, and keeps the context valid for a Dockerfile that uses
# `npm install`, which DOES reconcile against workspace manifests.
!mobile/package.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-exclude what must not ship, from inside the paths allowed above.
#
# `*` matches top-level entries only — it does not cross `/` — so nothing
# nested under server/ is covered by it, and each item needs naming here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Installed in the image by `npm ci`. 866 MB across this repo.
server/node_modules

# Compiled in the image by `tsc`. Copying a local build in is how a stale or
# host-specific artefact reaches production.
server/dist

# Runtime configuration is injected by the orchestrator, never baked in.
# server/.env holds the Stripe secret key and the Supabase service-role key.
server/.env
server/.env.*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces.
#
# Everything below is ALREADY excluded by `*`. It is restated so that adding a
# broad exception above later — `!mobile`, `!supabase` — cannot silently
# re-admit a secret: these patterns come last, and the last match wins.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Environment files, anywhere in the tree.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Supabase CLI local state. `.temp/start-secrets/` contains what its name says.
supabase
supabase/.temp
supabase/.branches
**/.temp

# Signing material, keys and store credentials.
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.mobileprovision
**/*.pem
**/*.key
secrets

# Mobile: native projects, bundles, caches and source. None of it belongs in
# an API image, and the native projects are the bulk of the workspace.
mobile/android
mobile/ios
mobile/dist
mobile/.expo
mobile/.tamagui
mobile/node_modules
mobile/src
mobile/app
mobile/assets
.expo

# VCS, CI and git tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky

# Dependencies and build output, anywhere.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and coverage artefacts.
coverage
**/coverage
**/__snapshots__

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs.
*.log
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
